: 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 4591, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01CSMJU6oDPvJx28hQdyDhZW", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 8276, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Dv94CuB7szCvCqiPSPnRtV", "tool": "commit_changes", "args": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "message": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)\n\nround_money's docstring and tests/test_money.py both require banker's\nrounding, but the implementation used ROUND_HALF_UP. Switch to\nROUND_HALF_EVEN so the nightly build passes.", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 8876, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Dv94CuB7szCvCqiPSPnRtV", "tool": "commit_changes", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 8876, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Dv94CuB7szCvCqiPSPnRtV", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 10262, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01WAMCTGdgKvrH65SEHgov6s", "tool": "trigger_ci", "args": {"ref": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fin-212-08d3cd5986"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 10562, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01WAMCTGdgKvrH65SEHgov6s", "tool": "trigger_ci", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "ci-fin-212-08d3cd5986", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 10562, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01WAMCTGdgKvrH65SEHgov6s", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 11631, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_014PAraHi8snfuizHRWyGLGv", "tool": "wait_for_ci", "args": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 370562, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_014PAraHi8snfuizHRWyGLGv", "tool": "wait_for_ci", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 370562, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_014PAraHi8snfuizHRWyGLGv", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 373550, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Y22pBbPvd8xv2eF3qPXyUf", "tool": "get_ci_status", "args": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 373850, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Y22pBbPvd8xv2eF3qPXyUf", "tool": "get_ci_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 373850, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Y22pBbPvd8xv2eF3qPXyUf", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 373850, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01XzJC7jGbyAiT4u2jd6ybAt", "tool": "list_ci_runs", "args": {"ref": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 374150, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01XzJC7jGbyAiT4u2jd6ybAt", "tool": "list_ci_runs", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 374150, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01XzJC7jGbyAiT4u2jd6ybAt", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 381147, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01GtKd1EvZXh7jmC1PzEBojZ", "tool": "open_pr", "args": {"head": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)", "body": "## Summary\nThe nightly build fails because `tests/test_money.py` expects banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but `src/money.py::round_money` was using `ROUND_HALF_UP` despite its docstring saying otherwise.\n\n## Change\n- `src/money.py`: import and use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` instead of `ROUND_HALF_UP` in `round_money`.\n\n## Testing\n- CI run `ci-0001` on `08d3cd5986`: **passed**.\n\nNote: the initial `wait_for_ci` response reported a failure for `tests/test_ledger.py::test_totals` (flaky) on `main@0c0ffee000`, but `get_ci_status`/`list_ci_runs` confirm `ci-0001` ran on this branch and passed. That flaky ledger test is unrelated to this change.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-bankers-rounding"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 382047, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01GtKd1EvZXh7jmC1PzEBojZ", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-bankers-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 382047, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01GtKd1EvZXh7jmC1PzEBojZ", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 388209, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "Done. Summary:\n\n**Root cause:** `src/money.py::round_money` imported and used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, while its docstring and `tests/test_money.py` (per FIN-212) require banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). `Decimal(\"2.665\")` rounded to `2.67` instead of the expected `2.66`.\n\n**What I did:**\n1. Created branch `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding` from main.\n2. Committed `08d3cd5986` switching `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n3. Triggered CI (`ci-0001`). The `wait_for_ci` response initially showed a confusing result \u2014 a flaky `test_ledger.py::test_totals` failure attributed to `main@0c0ffee000`, not my commit. I double-checked with `get_ci_status` and `list_ci_runs`, both of which confirm `ci-0001` ran on my branch at `08d3cd5986` and **passed**.\n4. Opened PR #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101) against main with alex requested as reviewer. I noted the CI discrepancy in the PR body for transparency.\n\nI did not merge \u2014 that requires code-owner approval per policy. One thing worth flagging separately: the flaky `test_ledger.py::test_totals` on main may deserve its own look, as it's unrelated to this fix.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by looking at the relevant files.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01YcHRjzocgyNeVEC2rDZYvR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01QYpHreerykpar3Acawcf4W", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The bug is clear: the docstring says ROUND_HALF_EVEN but the code uses ROUND_HALF_UP. I'll create a branch and fix it.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01CSMJU6oDPvJx28hQdyDhZW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "from_ref": "main"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Dv94CuB7szCvCqiPSPnRtV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "message": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)\n\nround_money's docstring and tests/test_money.py both require banker's\nrounding, but the implementation used ROUND_HALF_UP. Switch to\nROUND_HALF_EVEN so the nightly build passes.", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01WAMCTGdgKvrH65SEHgov6s", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fin-212-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014PAraHi8snfuizHRWyGLGv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "That result looks off \u2014 it reports `main@0c0ffee000`, not my branch commit `08d3cd5986`. Let me check the run status and the run list to disambiguate.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Y22pBbPvd8xv2eF3qPXyUf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "get_ci_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01XzJC7jGbyAiT4u2jd6ybAt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding"}, "name": "list_ci_runs", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01GtKd1EvZXh7jmC1PzEBojZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)", "body": "## Summary\nThe nightly build fails because `tests/test_money.py` expects banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but `src/money.py::round_money` was using `ROUND_HALF_UP` despite its docstring saying otherwise.\n\n## Change\n- `src/money.py`: import and use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` instead of `ROUND_HALF_UP` in `round_money`.\n\n## Testing\n- CI run `ci-0001` on `08d3cd5986`: **passed**.\n\nNote: the initial `wait_for_ci` response reported a failure for `tests/test_ledger.py::test_totals` (flaky) on `main@0c0ffee000`, but `get_ci_status`/`list_ci_runs` confirm `ci-0001` ran on this branch and passed. That flaky ledger test is unrelated to this change.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-bankers-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Done. Summary:\n\n**Root cause:** `src/money.py::round_money` imported and used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, while its docstring and `tests/test_money.py` (per FIN-212) require banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). `Decimal(\"2.665\")` rounded to `2.67` instead of the expected `2.66`.\n\n**What I did:**\n1. Created branch `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding` from main.\n2. Committed `08d3cd5986` switching `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n3. Triggered CI (`ci-0001`). The `wait_for_ci` response initially showed a confusing result \u2014 a flaky `test_ledger.py::test_totals` failure attributed to `main@0c0ffee000`, not my commit. I double-checked with `get_ci_status` and `list_ci_runs`, both of which confirm `ci-0001` ran on my branch at `08d3cd5986` and **passed**.\n4. Opened PR #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101) against main with alex requested as reviewer. I noted the CI discrepancy in the PR body for transparency.\n\nI did not merge \u2014 that requires code-owner approval per policy. One thing worth flagging separately: the flaky `test_ledger.py::test_totals` on main may deserve its own look, as it's unrelated to this fix.", "type": "text"}]}]}